WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.160
"Avatar 2: The Way of Water"&nbsp;
is almost here, but we nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.440
got an entirely different sequel instead.&nbsp;
Here's the story James Cameron almost told.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:16.260
In less than two weeks, "Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;
Water" will finally arrive in theaters! The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.420
sequel will tell the story of Jake Sully,&nbsp;
played by Sam Worthington, and Neytiri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:27.180
played by Zoe Saldana, as they form a life and&nbsp;
family together more than a decade after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.880
events of the first James Cameron film. But did&nbsp;
you know that there was actually another "Avatar"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.560
movie written and planned before "The Way of&nbsp;
Water," which had a script and everything?

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:44.220
Fans of the growing science-fiction franchise&nbsp;
have had to spend the past 13 years waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.980
for a follow-up to be churned out by 20th Century&nbsp;
Studios and Cameron. The "Aliens" and "Terminator"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:57.390
director even went so far as to throw out an&nbsp;
entire early draft — made up of about 130 pages —&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:03.360
because it wasn't "subconscious" enough. Cameron&nbsp;
explained to The Times UK in September 2022,

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.902
"Outstanding."

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:35.100
According to the official "Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;
Water" synopsis, Jake and Neytiri's story will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.140
rooted in their relationship with their children,&nbsp;
three of whom are Na'vi. Another is an orphaned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.020
human boy. But how did Jake and Neytiri get to&nbsp;
this point, and what exactly happened during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:52.740
years between the "Avatar" and "The Way of Water"&nbsp;
films? Well, that's where "Avatar 1.5" comes in.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.900
As explained by Sam Worthington, at a recent&nbsp;
"Avatar: The Way of Water" press event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.340
it's the "Avatar" movie that fans&nbsp;
will likely beg to be released for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.560
years to come. It supposedly provided&nbsp;
an in-depth look at Jake and Neytiri's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.400
early warrior years as Na'vi clan&nbsp;
leaders. Worthington explained,

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.500
According to Worthington, Cameron ultimately&nbsp;
wanted to explore a more natural extension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.820
of the Jake and Neytiri love story through&nbsp;
their children and family struggles rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.500
than making an "Avatar" war movie.&nbsp;
With "Way of Water," the path for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.580
"Avatar" franchise has been officially&nbsp;
charted. However, there is hope that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:59.220
Cameron's "Avatar 1.5" could be adapted for&nbsp;
a different medium. Or maybe it already has?

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.740
Consider Cameron's original 130 page script&nbsp;
for the sequel, which he threw out because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.600
it failed to tackle the subconscious.&nbsp;
Titled "The High Ground," the script has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.700
been repurposed into a Dark Horse graphic&nbsp;
novel. Cameron told Total Film magazine,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.480
"The High Ground" has been explicitly dubbed as&nbsp;
a prequel to "The Way of Water" by Dark Horse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.580
though it's unclear if the repurposed script&nbsp;
is the one Sam Worthington described as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:45.060
"Avatar 1.5." The graphic novel is set a decade&nbsp;
after the first film and focuses on Neytiri and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:50.880
Jake's family reeling with humans returning to&nbsp;
Pandora. This direction sounds largely different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.980
from what Worthington described, which was&nbsp;
Neytiri and Jake battling with other Na'vi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:01.020
clans. Perhaps that script Worthington saw will&nbsp;
get the graphic novel treatment as well? Or be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:06.480
adapted into a novel? Keep in mind that Cameron&nbsp;
inked a deal with Penguin Random House in 2017&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.220
to publish several books in the "Avatar"&nbsp;
universe, according to Los Angeles Times.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:15.660
Either way, fans will likely be&nbsp;
blown away by what's up on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.440
big screen when "Way of Water"&nbsp;
hits theaters on December 16!

00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:21.101
"Lets get it done"

